From 67a1ffe54cf341fa4b505638a3b6460056e5b0dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:13:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(ui): preview and trash snapshots in the recent
 snapshots list

- Each row of the Recent list shows a thumbnail of the snapshot (its first
  camera's color image). Clicking it opens a full-screen dialog with all of
  its images side by side, every camera's color image and colorized depth
  (<cam>.depth_preview.png) where there is one, captioned "<camera>, color" /
  "<camera>, depth", and its label, comment, capture time and environment.
  Closing it goes back to the list.
- A trash button per row asks first, in a modal alert dialog (Cancel has
  focus; Enter and Escape act on the dialog, not on the episode hotkeys), then
  moves the snapshot to the trash on the backend. A toast says where it went
  (and if the CSV lags behind), and the list is fetched again; after a failure
  too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
